{"id": "q0067", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1665173357, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "James likes to check the coin return of the vending machine for change. One day he finds a quarter, two nickels, and 7 dimes. How much money in cents does James have?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0067.wav", "input_sha256": "21a8f15b9712d79881367142340f215c527203a49062e0eafa76a4efb920b66e", "input_samples": 220400, "input_s": 13.775, "n_real_chunks": 14, "score": 0.1884, "act": 0.9985, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So let's add up the coins James found. He has a quarter, which is 2 5 cents, two nickels, which are 5 cents each, so that' s 10 cents total for the nickels, and seven dimes, which are 10 cents each, so that's 70 cents from the dimes. Now, adding them all together: 2 5 cents from the quarter, plus 1 0 cents from the nickels, plus 7 0 cents from the di mes gives us 105 cents in total.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 13, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 24, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0067_local_local.wav", "sha256": "b5bf1357d0b0b542aa260f92ea8d83fe4155e39690c139df7a1b627007c5bfc4", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 24.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.061, 1.11, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.062, 2.111, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.062, 3.111, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.0