{"id": "q0115", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3284998833, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "In the land of Ink, the money system is unique. One Trinket is equal to 4 Blinkets, and 3 Blinkets are equal to 7 Drinkets. In Trinkets, what is the value of 56 Drinkets?\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0115.wav", "input_sha256": "425f92be59171877dec281c6414f9619dfde45f63ec7c9755b417a80bd6f497e", "input_samples": 209600, "input_s": 13.1, "n_real_chunks": 14, "score": 0.4078, "act": 0.9981, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so we' re told that 1 trinket is equal to 4 blankets. And then also that 3 blankets are equal to 7 drink its. So let's start by figuring out how many blankets are in one drinkit. If 3 blankets equal 7 drinkits, then one blanket must be 7 divided by 3 drinkits. So that would be about 2.3 3 drinkits per blanket. Now, since 1 trinket equals 4 blankets, and each blanket is worth about 2.3 3 drinkits, we can multiply 4 by 2.33 to find out how many drinkits are in one trinket. Let me do the math here. 4 times 2.33 is roughly 9.3 2 drinkits per trinket. So now, if we have 56 drinkits, we just divide that by the value of one trinket in drinkits to get the equivalent in trinkets. 56 divided by 9.3 2 gives us approximately 6 trinkets.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 13, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 47, "feed_lag_max_ms": 28, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 28, 