{"id": "q0149", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3071058655, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "If we write $\\sqrt{2}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} + \\sqrt{3} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ in the form $\\dfrac{a\\sqrt{2} + b\\sqrt{3}}{c}$ such that $a$, $b$, and $c$ are positive integers and $c$ is as small as possible, then what is $a+b+c$?\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0149.wav", "input_sha256": "1aba5f1aa218ea4829a3402ef44d24088c12e578440003f61eac5b024f65f75e", "input_samples": 267400, "input_s": 16.712, "n_real_chunks": 17, "score": 0.9358, "act": 0.9975, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so we' ve got this expression here, and it looks like a mess. But the first thing I notice is that there are two square roots in the de nominator of the fraction. So maybe if I rational ize them, then things will get better. And to do that, I'm going to multiply the top and bottom by the conjugate of the denominator. That's just going to be the same as changing the sign on the second term. So that would be square root 2 minus square root 3 divided by square root 2 plus square root 3. So now when I multip ly these together, I get a difference of square s in the deno minator. So square root 2 squared is just 2, and square root 3 squared is 3. So that means the deno minator is negative 1. The next step is to multiply the top and bottom by the conju gate of the new deno minator, which is just going to change the sign on the second term again. So I'll have square root 2 plus square root 3 over negative 1. Now all I need to do is combine like terms. So that gives me 1 over negative 1 times square root 2 plus square root 3. So I can rewrite this as negative 1 times square root 2 plus square root 3. And now I see that the form they want matches exactly what", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 14, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 60, "feed_lag_max_ms": 61, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 61, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0149_local_local.wav", "sha256": "a0dd25eb319efe7098ae31a736bc2fdc250de6af0413ad9519b588c8acdef56c", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 60.0}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.068, 1.122, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.069, 2.122, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.07, 3.123, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.07, 4.126, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.072, 5.128, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.07, 6.126, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.074, 7.133, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.072, 8.128, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.071, 9.127, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.072, 10.127, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.072, 11.128, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.072, 12.128, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.073, 13.128, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.073, 14.128, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.074, 15.624, 0, 24000, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.074, 16.774, 0, 24000, 0], [16, 1, 16.712, 16.846, 17.437, 0, 24000, 0], [17, 0, 17.712, 17.787, 18.461, 0, 24000, 0], [18, 0, 18.712, 18.786, 19.431, 0, 24000, 0], [19, 0, 19.712, 19.787, 20.52, 0, 24000, 0], [20, 0, 20.712, 20.786, 21.457, 0, 24000, 0], [21, 0, 21.712, 21.789, 22.517, 0, 24000, 0], [22, 0, 22.712, 22.787, 23.426, 0, 24000, 0], [23, 0, 23.712, 23.787, 24.456, 0, 24000, 0], [24, 0, 24.712, 24.788, 25.511, 0, 24000, 0], [25, 0, 25.712, 25.79, 26.41, 0, 24000, 0], [26, 0, 26.712, 26.789, 27.491, 0, 24000, 0], [27, 0, 27.712, 27.793, 28.471, 0, 24000, 0], [28, 0, 28.712, 28.789, 29.437, 0, 24000, 0], [29, 0, 29.712, 29.787, 30.465, 0, 24000, 0], [30, 0, 30.712, 30.786, 31.509, 0, 2