{"id": "q0234", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2226845436, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "Fernandez is planning to attend an auction of the assets of Cross & Black, one of his major competitors who is liquidating. In the conduct of the auction, which of the following rules applies?\n\nA. A bidder can retract his bid even after the fall of the hammer.\nB. If the auction is with reserve, the auctioneer cannot withdraw the article at any time.\nC. The retraction of a bid by a bidder automatically ends the auction.\nD. A bidder may retract his bid at any time until the falling of the hammer.\nE. The auctioneer can increase the bidding price at any time during the auction.\nF. If the auction is without reserve, the auctioneer can withdraw the article at any time prior to the fall of the hammer.\nG. All bids are final and cannot be retracted under any circumstances.\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0234.wav", "input_sha256": "e662b2a591353a619903555c94c49e65ea45bd92dd186a9a270cf319b533006b", "input_samples": 822400, "input_s": 51.4, "n_real_chunks": 52, "score": 0.6802, "act": 0.9997, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So, let's go through the options. A says a bidder can re tract his bid even after the fall of the hammer that's not true once the hammer falls the bid is final. B says if the auction is with reserve the auction e er cannot withdraw the article at any time. That' s also not correct. If there's a reserve, the auctioneer can still withdraw it if the price doesn't meet the minimum. C says the re traction of a bid automatically ends the auction. No, retract ing a bid doesn't end the auction; it just cancel s that specific bid. D says a bidder may retract his bid at any time until the falling of the hammer. Yes, this is generally true. Before the hammer falls, bidders can usually cancel their bids. E says the auction eer can increase the bi dding price at any time during the auction. Usually no, the auctioneer typically only announces the next bid based on what bidders say. So, the correct answer is D: a bidder may re tract his bid at any time until the falling of the hammer.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 35, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 50, "feed_lag_max_ms": 407, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 590, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0234_local_local.wav", "sha256": "307563734ffefe03450818ba5b7b2ce1c45055a05a61d94426cbe9d24bc6c150", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 49.72}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.068, 1.122, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.07, 2.124, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.068, 3.121, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.07, 4.125, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.071, 5.126, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.07, 6.125, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.07, 7.125, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.073, 8.129, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.071, 9.126, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.073, 10.13, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.073, 11.129, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.073, 12.13, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.073, 13.129, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.076, 14.132, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.082, 15.142, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.076, 16.133, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.075, 17.132, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.077, 18.133, 1, 0, 0], [18, 1, 19.0, 19.076, 19.132, 1, 0, 0], [19, 1, 20.0, 20.075, 20.13, 1, 0, 0], [20, 1, 21.0, 21.076, 21.132, 1, 0, 0], [21, 1, 22.0, 22.076, 22.132, 1, 0, 0], [22, 1, 23.0, 23.077, 23.133, 1, 0, 0], [23, 1, 24.0, 24.077, 24.133