{"id": "q0524", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2565787960, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "分压电路的原理是什么？", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0524.wav", "input_sha256": "9041d8d0d09801aedb3910612edd66003b9535800d8e50ece31e0dc01f31e2d5", "input_samples": 27800, "input_s": 1.738, "n_real_chunks": 2, "score": 0.2436, "act": 0.9844, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "分压电路呢是通过电阻的串联来实现电压分配的。其原理就是利用欧姆定律和基尔霍夫电压定律，当多个电阻串联时，总电压会被各个电阻按比例分配。具体来说，每个电阻两端的电压降与该电阻的阻值成正比。也就是说，阻值大的电阻会获得更大的电压，而阻值小的电阻则获得较小的电压。所以通过调整电阻的大小或数量，就可以得到不同的输出电压，这在需要稳定低电压的电路中非常常见。", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 38, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0524_local_local.wav", "sha256": "bc4d2f33c30e61403a035d3fe1a609a8d0d9902b33445d115e5a4b496c885786", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 37.68}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.07, 1.125, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 1.738, 1.808, 1.861, 1, 0, 0], [2, 0, 2.737, 2.806, 2.859, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.737, 3.807, 4.432, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.737, 4.809, 5.454, 0, 24000, 0], [5, 0, 5.737, 5.808, 6.454, 0, 24000, 0], [6, 0, 6.737, 6.809, 7.485, 0, 24000, 0], [7, 0, 7.737, 7.808, 8.402, 0, 24000, 0], [8, 0, 8.738, 8.81, 9.487, 0, 24000, 0], [9, 0, 9.738, 9.81, 10.461, 0, 24000, 0], [10, 0, 10.738, 10.81, 11.425, 0, 24000, 0], [11, 0, 11.738, 11.811, 12.371, 0, 24000, 0], [12, 0, 12.738, 12.811, 13.491, 0, 24000, 0], [13, 0,